From d31c61cfce072dd830625366751ae8334cf16f9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ferdinand Vanmaele <info@fvanmaele.de>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:13:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [clangd] Index navigation: a reindexed TU rewrites its shard;
 no answer while it is queued

A header changed on disk while clangd was not running: at the next start
the main file's shard still passed its own digest check, and navigation
from the index answered with references resolved against the old header,
also after the reindex, which writes only shards whose digest changed
(S23 case 1a).

- The main file is always collected (FileFilter) and its shard always
  rewritten by a reindex (BackgroundIndex::update).
- The TUs loadProject queues for reindexing are marked before navigation
  from the index may answer (waitForLoadedShards now waits for the
  staleness check); a marked TU's index answer is declined until its
  reindex is in the served index (BackgroundIndexRebuilder::indexedTU
  numbers each indexed TU, servedTUs() says which the served version
  holds), or for the session if its reindex failed
  (BackgroundIndex::reindexPending).
- The staleness check reads the loaded files in parallel (llvm::parallelFor):
  it is now on the path of the first navigation. 2661 files of a deal.II
  TU: 3.9 s one by one on a Mac with an on-access scanner.

ClangdTests 1436/1436 (new: StaleTUWaitsForItsServedReindex,
ServedTUsFollowTheServedVersion; the first fails without the change).
S23 case 1a through LSP: the AST answers right in the session after the
change, the index right in the next.

Not handled: upstream queues one TU per stale file (its DependentTU), so
other TUs including a changed header are neither reindexed nor marked.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
